From: box86-16k contributors
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] LIBC: emulate 4K guest madvise on larger host pages

The Box64 non-4K protection work in 9c11c567 also wrapped madvise(2),
because an i386 guest may issue advice on a 4K-aligned range that is not
aligned to the host's 16K page size.  The original Box86 16K port carried the
mprotect half of that change but omitted madvise.

Keep guest 4K alignment semantics, round non-destructive host advice to host
pages, and emulate unaligned MADV_DONTNEED for writable anonymous guest mmap
regions by zeroing only the requested guest pages.  Track file-backed guest
mmap regions separately so the fallback never overwrites file-backed data.
Also route the raw i386 madvise syscall through the same wrapper.
